      },
      "cr": 0.125,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Speaker Rivers.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. XP ledger: level 1, power rating 2 → CR 1/8 as a noble. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Trojan Speaker</strong> — Liberated Toads</p><p>Status: Active — assumed direction of the movement after Speaker L's disappearance</p><p>Rivers resigned from the Midlands Diet at 09:00 on the 21st of Highsun, 1040 BF in protest at the Iron Mandate, then allowed himself to be taken so that a digital virus could be carried inside Aegis Command. He is credited in the battle record with triggering the largest prison break in Regal Empire history, and with directing it remotely. Where Speaker L argued, Rivers acts, and the archive is not yet agreed on whether that is an improvement.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Cane</strong> — “The Trojan Speaker”</li><li><strong>Hidden in Plain Sight</strong> — “This wasn't some clumsy error of judgment—it was a deliberate infiltration of Aegis Command.”</li><li><strong>Cooks for an Army</strong> — “The atmosphere in the Diet was suffocating; it was a pressure cooker of legislation where two massive pieces of law, the Supernatural Sovereignty Act and the Iron Mandate, were shoved through the system in a frantic”</li><li><strong>Coin Sense</strong> — “Where Speaker L argued, Rivers acts, and the archive is not yet agreed on whether that is an improvement.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/speaker_rivers</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/speaker_rivers</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
